    "created_at": "2016-10-27T12:49:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-27T12:49:44Z",
    "body": "This is a bit messy. In Gecko by default all the default handlers are called, but things like link activation sets an internal 'default prevented' to true and that makes only the innermost link to be followed.\nBut I can definitely see inconsistencies in the code.\n\nWe need plenty of tests here, I'm afraid, and then decide what to spec.\n\nI wonder how other browsers deal with this, since also there in some cases inner most activatable element is triggered (nested <a>) but in some cases outermost. @dtapuska \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
